  "instructions": [
    "Preheat ttukbaegi-earthenware-cook to 300°F.",
    "Season pork with fish sauce, lime juice, grated ginger, chili flakes, brown sugar, garlic powder, and black pepper.",
    "Heat coconut oil in the earthenware-cook over medium-high heat.",
    "Grill pork in batches until browned on all sides and cooked through, about 4 minutes per batch.",
    "Transfer pork to a plate and let rest for 2 minutes.",
    "Meanwhile, toast Thai basil and mint leaves in the earthenware-cook until fragrant.",
    "Serve pork with sticky rice, toasted herbs, and your choice of toppings.",
    "Garnish with additional Thai basil and mint leaves, if desired."
